218-- **Performance activity:** **Listening:** Identify what happened, how each person felt, and what change is promised.
219-
220:### Lesson 15 — Do You Know Whether the Laundry Room Is Free?
221-
222-- **Module:** 3 — Neighbours, requests, and mutual help
223-- **Real-life situation:** Asking a neighbour for information that may be uncertain.
224-- **Can do:** I can ask indirectly whether a simple fact is true.
225-- **Primary language structure:** Indirect yes/no questions with `ob` and final verb position.
226-- **Sentence functions practised:** Indirect question; uncertainty; answer; offer of help.
227-- **Target passage:** Hallway dialogue; 5 turns; about 72–80 words.
228-- **Connectedness:** Each turn narrows one practical question about access and timing.
229-- **New vocabulary or chunks:** `ob`; `wissen`; `die Waschküche`; `frei sein`; `die Hausordnung`; `der Hausmeister`; `nachsehen`.
230-- **Deliberately recycled:** yes/no questions and time (A1 L4, L10–L12); home and services (A1 L19–L24); polite forms (L13); subordinate word order (L3).
231-- **Performance activity:** **Writing:** Turn three direct yes/no questions into short indirect enquiries beginning with `Wissen Sie …?`.
232-
233-### Lesson 16 — I Can Help Him
234-
235-- **Module:** 3 — Neighbours, requests, and mutual help
236-- **Real-life situation:** Offering practical help to different people in the building.
237-- **Can do:** I can understand and use common dative pronouns for the person receiving help.
238-- **Primary language structure:** Dative personal pronouns `mir`, `dir`, `ihm`, `ihr`, `uns`, `euch`, and `Ihnen` with common verbs.
239-- **Sentence functions practised:** Offer; request; acceptance; report about another person.
240-- **Target passage:** Short multi-person exchange; 6 turns; about 74–82 words.
241-- **Connectedness:** The same task passes between speakers, making each pronoun’s referent recoverable from context.
242-- **New vocabulary or chunks:** `leihen`; `gehören`; `bringen`; `das Werkzeug`; `die Leiter`; `der Eimer`; `jemandem helfen`.
243-- **Deliberately recycled:** dative `mir` (A1 L31–L32); help/service language (A1 L21, L35–L36); people and possessives; neighbour problems (L13–L15).
244-- **Performance activity:** **Listening:** Match each offered object or action to the person who receives it.
245-
246-### Lesson 17 — Give Her the Package, Please
247-
248-- **Module:** 3 — Neighbours, requests, and mutual help
249-- **Real-life situation:** Passing objects and messages to neighbours who are not home.
250-- **Can do:** I can state who receives something and what is transferred.
251-- **Primary language structure:** Dative recipient before an accusative noun object in common transfer patterns such as `jemandem etwas geben`.
252-- **Sentence functions practised:** Request; transfer; message relay; confirmation.
253-- **Target passage:** Delivery exchange; 5–6 turns; about 74–84 words.
254-- **Connectedness:** One package and one message are tracked across speaker, temporary receiver, and final recipient.

